{"message":"I can help with this. Based on the available product information, the strongest checking option for premium perks appears to be the Bluest Account: 2.25% APY, 10 complimentary domestic outgoing wires monthly, no fee for incoming domestic wires, a dedicated personal banker, up to $50 in monthly ATM-fee rebates, three complimentary check orders yearly, no stop-payment fee, and no Rho-Bank foreign ATM fee. However, its benefits require a $75,000 opening deposit and a $112,500 minimum daily balance, so your $100,000 savings would not meet that ongoing threshold if used to fund it.

For savings, the personal Gold Account has a documented 5.5% base APY and requires a $5,000 opening deposit and $10,000 ongoing balance. Pairing it with a Green Account checking account adds a documented 0.75% boost, for a potential 6.25% APY before any eligible credit-card or relationship bonuses. The Green Account has a $22.50 monthly fee, waived with a $1,350 minimum daily balance. The Platinum Plus Account accepts your $100,000 amount and requires a $100,000 ongoing balance, but its base APY was not included in the product information I found, so I cannot honestly confirm whether it beats the documented Gold-plus-Green combination. Checking boosts do not stack.

Before I can look up your accounts, close Light Blue, or open new accounts, I need to verify your identity. Please provide any two of these four items exactly as they appear on your profile: date of birth, email address, phone number, or mailing address. Also confirm whether you want me to prioritize the highest savings APY or the best checking perks if one checking option cannot satisfy both goals."}

